### AI Voice Agent — Dashboard API
### Run top to bottom from IntelliJ's gutter icons; the token and ids are captured for you.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### Health
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- AUTH

### Login as the bootstrap admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@vedryxtech.com",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Who am I
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Current organization and its call policy
GET {{api}}/organizations/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Retune the retry rules (ORG_ADMIN)
PUT {{api}}/organizations/current/call-policy
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxAttempts": 5,
  "maxAttemptsPerDay": 3,
  "retryBackoffMinutes": {
    "noAnswer": 90,
    "busy": 20,
    "rejected": 1440,
    "voicemail": 240,
    "failed": 10
  },
  "callingWindowStart": "09:30",
  "callingWindowEnd": "19:30",
  "recordingEnabled": true
}

### Add an agent user
POST {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agent@vedryxtech.com",
  "password": "Agent@12345",
  "fullName": "Floor Agent",
  "roles": ["agent"]
}

### No token -> 401
GET {{api}}/leads

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- LEADS

### Create a FRESH lead - all it takes is a name and a number.
### It is queued for a call straight away. No action fields: the call produces those.
POST {{api}}/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Shrikant",
  "phone": "+919000000101",
  "project": "My Home Sanctuary",
  "source": "website",
  "campaign": "sanctuary-launch"
}

> {% client.global.set("leadId", response.body.id); %}

### Import a lead that was already worked elsewhere - the action fields are
### accepted here too, and each action type requires its own time.
POST {{api}}/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Dev",
  "phone": "+919000000102",
  "project": "My Home Sanctuary",
  "actionType": "siteVisit",
  "scheduledFor": "2026-09-05T10:00:00+05:30",
  "reminderEnabled": true,
  "notes": "Lead explicitly confirmed the site-visit date and time."
}

### Duplicate phone number -> 409
POST {{api}}/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "phone": "+91 90000 00101"
}

### Upsert — same number, newer action
PUT {{api}}/leads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Shrikant",
  "phone": "+919000000101",
  "project": "My Home Sanctuary",
  "source": "walk-in"
}

### List — pending work only
GET {{api}}/leads?pipelineStatus=queued&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List — converted leads
GET {{api}}/leads?finalStatus=siteVisitBooked
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List — leads with a recording
GET {{api}}/leads?hasRecording=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Find by phone through the list endpoint
GET {{api}}/leads?phone=+919000000101
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Partial update
PATCH {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Reviewed by the sales desk.",
  "assignedTo": "floor-agent-1"
}

### Manual suppression (stops the dialler immediately)
PATCH {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "doNotCall": true
}

### Put a lead back in the queue
PATCH {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pipelineStatus": "queued",
  "doNotCall": false
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- CALLS

### How much work is due right now
GET {{api}}/call-queue
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dialler claims a batch (atomic)
POST {{api}}/call-queue/claims?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

> {% if (response.body.length > 0) {
       client.global.set("callLogId", response.body[0].callLogId);
       client.global.set("callLeadId", response.body[0].leadId);
     } %}

### Call one lead now (idempotent on the key)
POST {{api}}/leads/{{leadId}}/calls
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotencyKey": "worker-1-attempt-abc123",
  "handledBy": "ai_agent"
}

### Hangup — NO ANSWER -> retry with backoff, inside the calling window
POST {{api}}/calls/{{callLogId}}/outcome
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "noAnswer",
  "ringSeconds": 25
}

### Hangup — ANSWERED, site visit booked -> lead closes as converted
POST {{api}}/calls/{{callLogId}}/outcome
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "answered",
  "disposition": "siteVisitBooked",
  "talkSeconds": 214,
  "siteVisitAt": "2026-09-06T11:00:00+05:30",
  "summary": "Wants the 3 BHK; visiting Saturday.",
  "recordingUrl": "https://recordings.local/call-abc.mp3",

  "leadName": "Shrikant Giri",
  "leadProject": "My Home Sanctuary",
  "leadQuery": "Can 2 BHK and 3 BHK be combined to make 5 BHK?",
  "whatsappPhone": "+919876543210"
}

### Hangup — ANSWERED, wants a callback -> booked, no attempt spent
POST {{api}}/calls/{{callLogId}}/outcome
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "answered",
  "disposition": "callbackRequested",
  "talkSeconds": 41,
  "requestedCallbackAt": "2026-09-02T18:30:00+05:30",
  "summary": "Busy, asked for Tuesday evening."
}

### Hangup — ANSWERED, do not call -> suppressed for good
POST {{api}}/calls/{{callLogId}}/outcome
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "answered",
  "disposition": "doNotCall",
  "talkSeconds": 12
}

### Callback with no time -> 422
POST {{api}}/calls/{{callLogId}}/outcome
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "answered",
  "disposition": "callbackRequested"
}

### Reschedule outside a call — 23:30 gets clamped to the next 09:00
POST {{api}}/leads/{{callLeadId}}/call-reschedules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requestedAt": "2026-09-03T23:30:00+05:30",
  "notes": "Lead asked for late night; pushed into the calling window."
}

### Free leads abandoned mid-call by a dead worker
POST {{api}}/call-queue/recoveries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------- FOLLOW-UP HISTORY

### Full attempt history for one lead
GET {{api}}/leads/{{callLeadId}}/calls
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Searchable call log
GET {{api}}/calls?outcome=noAnswer&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One attempt with its event timeline
GET {{api}}/calls/{{callLogId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --------------------------------------------------------------- RECORDINGS

### Everything with a playable recording
GET {{api}}/calls/recordings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Playback URL for one attempt
GET {{api}}/calls/{{callLogId}}/recording
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------- DASHBOARD

### Everything the landing page needs
GET {{api}}/dashboard/summary?range=month
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------- AI AGENT (API KEY)
### The voice-agent application uses a key instead of logging in.
### The default key is created on first start; rotate it with the endpoint below.

@apiKey = <BOOTSTRAP_API_KEY from your .env>

### Agent reads the lead list - no login involved
GET {{api}}/leads?size=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Agent pushes in a fresh lead to be called
POST {{api}}/leads
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Captured By Agent",
  "phone": "+919000000222",
  "project": "My Home Sanctuary",
  "source": "inbound-call"
}

### Agent takes work from the queue
POST {{api}}/call-queue/claims?limit=3
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

> {% if (response.body.length > 0) {
       client.global.set("agentCallLogId", response.body[0].callLogId);
     } %}

### Agent reports the call, attaching the recording link
POST {{api}}/calls/{{agentCallLogId}}/outcome
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "answered",
  "disposition": "siteVisitBooked",
  "talkSeconds": 186,
  "siteVisitAt": "2026-09-07T11:00:00+05:30",
  "summary": "Booked Saturday visit.",
  "recordingUrl": "https://recordings.local/call-abc.mp3",

  "leadName": "Shrikant Giri",
  "leadProject": "My Home Sanctuary",
  "leadQuery": "Asked about floor plans and payment schedule"
}

### A wrong key is refused
GET {{api}}/leads
X-API-Key: vdx_not_a_real_key

### The agent cannot manage users (403)
POST {{api}}/users
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nope@vedryxtech.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "fullName": "Should Fail",
  "roles": ["agent"]
}

### ------------------------------------------------------- API KEY MANAGEMENT (ADMIN)

### Show which key is in use (prefix only - the key itself cannot be read back)
GET {{api}}/api-keys/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rotate the key. The full key is in this response and nowhere else - copy it.
### The previous key stops working immediately.
POST {{api}}/api-keys/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Revoke the key entirely
DELETE {{api}}/api-keys/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
